%PROPERTIES
Unimodular=1
%REFERENCES
I. Gauvin, Even unimodular ideal lattices of rank 88 over Q(zeta_115), preprint, 15 October 2026 (arXiv identifier pending),
and its addendum: two further extremal lattices, X4969 and X4049 (October 2026).
Data, programs and certificates: https://github.com/Katabolanga/rang88-reseaux-ideaux
%NOTES
The two generators span a subgroup of the automorphism group, hence the catalogue sections SUBGROUP_ORDER, SUBGROUP_NAME and SUBGROUP_GENERATORS; the full automorphism group is not known.
SUBGROUP_NAME: C115 : C4 = <zeta> : <g2>, zeta of order 115, g2 of order 4 with g2^2 = -1 and g2^-1 zeta g2 = zeta^24 (C4 acts through C2); equivalently C23 x Dic5.
X4969 = (P, b), an ideal lattice over L = Q(zeta), zeta = zeta_115 (rank 88): P = (4969, zeta^2 + 3763*zeta + 2809) is a prime ideal
of Z[zeta] of residue degree 2, and b(u, v) = Tr_{L/Q}(alpha u conj(v)), alpha = beta_0/nu totally positive (see the paper, section 6).
Minimum 8 is established by the computer-assisted method of the paper (same certifying program, same execution model of section 5.4:
M1, M2, H1-H3), as reported in the addendum: both sides of the criterion were swept completely, each side twice on two different
machines, with byte-identical receipts and no hit. The attached Python scripts check the exported matrices and generators, not the minimum.
The kissing number 168498000 follows from that minimum-8 statement and the extremal theta series.
Basis: an LLL-reduced Z-basis of P; X4969_construction.gp gives it in the power basis of Z[zeta], together with alpha.
Generators (row convention, g*GRAM*g^T = GRAM): g1 = multiplication by -zeta, of order 230;
g2 = the semilinear map u -> lambda*sigma_24(u), sigma_24(zeta) = zeta^24, lambda a unit of Z[zeta] (in X4969_construction.gp);
g2^2 = -1, and g2 o g1 o g2^(-1) = g1^139 as maps (in matrices: g2^(-1)*g1*g2 = g1^139).
<g1, g2> has order 460 = 2^2*5*23: an extension of the Galois stabiliser <sigma_24> (order 2) of the class of P by the cyclic group
<-zeta> (order 230). By the normaliser argument of the paper (Remark 2.6) and the stabiliser of the class (support {3,331}, see the
addendum), it is the normaliser in Aut of the group of multiplications by roots of unity. The full automorphism group has not been
determined: |Aut| >= 460.
A vector of norm 8 (transported to this basis), as a row of coordinates in this basis:
NORM8: 100 151 118 -34 -57 -37 -21 3 12 53 -4 0 -87 -24 -65 -9 -25 50 -106 59 61 16 -19 -48 -19 -60 7 -29 11 -32 20 14 15 -20 -5 25 -18 12 -1 -10 7 7 -2 -6 -4 10 -11 10 -11 0 -8 -10 -7 7 5 1 0 1 -2 -7 -3 0 8 0 -1 -6 -1 -3 -2 5 4 5 -3 -3 3 4 1 0 -2 0 1 0 2 4 0 2 0 -2
